A database through four deploys, as a team's work reaches it:

1. `title` renamed `name` (a @drop and a @from).
2. A teammate's branch, merged after: a `note` column. The rename's lines
   are still in schema.sql and do nothing.
3. A UNIQUE added on `name`: a rebuild, the rows copied by name.
4. The rename's lines removed, every database having passed them.

Each deploy plans only its own change; the rows survive all four.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup', 95), (2, 'bread', 40);

== after
-- @drop column dish title
-- @from column dish name = title
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT;

== after
-- @drop column dish title
-- @from column dish name = title
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;

== after
-- @drop column dish title
-- @from column dish name = title
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;

== query
SELECT id, name, price_kr, note FROM dish ORDER BY id

== plan
-- after 1
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `dish`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "dish" RENAME TO "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT
  table `dish`: its rows, by id, name = title, price_kr
    INSERT INTO "dish" ("id", "name", "price_kr") SELECT "id", (
    title
    ), "price_kr" FROM "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_dish"
